WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.500
Welcome to Process Management. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Steer organizational process improvement using evidence and business priorities.

2
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:20.240
Consider this scenario. Improvement suggestions remain unreviewed for a year. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:29.840
Start with two steps: Identify performance gaps. Then Prioritize improvements. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:39.050
Continue with Pilot and deploy changes. Then Measure benefits and refine. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:59.610
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous improvement backlog, decisions, effectiveness results tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: treating compliance checklists as the whole improvement strategy; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:13.860
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
